<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Tanganyika</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Tanganyika is a long, deep lake in the African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-rift">Great Rift Valley</a>, bordered by present-day Tanzania, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>, Burundi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>. Under rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumwimbe-ngombe">Kumwimbe Ngombe</a>, military expeditions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a> extended eastward towards the lake. The region connected Luba to wider trade networks reaching the East African coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika.jpg" alt="Lake Tanganyika" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS51G-034-0012_Lake_Tanganyika_June1985.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
